Carafe: with the profiler on, the runtime passes FEX_GDBSYMBOLS=1 whatever the program's settings say. FEX then
records every x86 instruction in a block's RIP map, which the profiler needs to name the guest code it samples; without
the profiler the option keeps its setting, off by default.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/horizon-wine/source/runtime.c
+++ b/horizon-wine/source/runtime.c
@@ -1734,6 +1734,7 @@
 
         if (launcher_kv_get( &kv, option->name, configured, sizeof(configured) ) &&
             nx_fex_option_choice( option, configured ) >= 0) value = configured;
+        if (option->id == NX_FEX_GDB_SYMBOLS && runtime_profile) value = "1";
         length = snprintf( buffer + used, size - used, "%s=%s", option->name, value );
         if (length < 0 || (size_t)length + 1 > size - used) return 0;
         used += length + 1;
